An original Zig implementation
------------------------------

The block and frame codecs implement the two format documents of the LZ4
project, `doc/lz4_Block_format.md` and `doc/lz4_Frame_format.md` (LZ4
v1.10.0, Yann Collet), as the specification. The compressor is a textbook
single-probe hash-table greedy LZ77 matcher with LZ4's published
"acceleration" skip; no liblz4 code was copied or translated.

Design references consulted for BEHAVIOUR only (which inputs are accepted or
refused), no code copied:

  - liblz4 v1.10.0 `lib/lz4.c`, `LZ4_decompress_generic` (BSD-2-Clause): the
    validity conditions of its safe decoding loop, to decide which of the
    format's optional end-of-block rules this module enforces (SPEC.md
    "Behaviour choices").
  - lz4_flex `src/frame/decompress.rs` (MIT, https://github.com/PSeitz/lz4_flex):
    its handling of concatenated frames, dictionary ids and oversized blocks.

Black-box test oracles
----------------------

The `lz4` command-line program (v1.10.0; the program is GPL-2.0-or-later, the
library BSD-2-Clause) and python-lz4 4.4.5 (BSD-3-Clause, linking the system
liblz4) are run as black boxes by `tools/interop.zig` and `tools/bench.zig`.
The frames in `src/testdata/` are the CLI's output over inputs this module's
recipe generates (`tools/capture-goldens.sh`): our content in the tool's
format, which needs no attribution (root NOTICE §0); recorded here with the
version for reproducibility. No source of the CLI was read.
